  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TBL Dairy: Securing production capacity through a Talent Development Programme for employees in Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">There is a growing demand in Kenya for high quality dairy products, such as yoghurt drinks, ice and pasteurized milk. Dutch company The Blue Link (TBL) and its Kenyan subsidiary Bio Food Products ltd invested in a dairy factory in Nairobi which is now being upgraded to the latest industry standards through finance from DGGF and the Rabobank.TBL is rapidly growing, a 45% growth rate in 2017, and this growth is also visible in the number of employees. Technical Assistance through DGGF was provided to enable further and professional growth of the dairy factory and to minimise risks of the investments. The TA included 1) the set-up of an efficient HRM system, 2) the development and implementation of a &#x2018;Talent Development Program&#x2019; to retain staff and promote personal and professional development and 3) a culture change program to secure further growth of the dairy factory.  The project was successful and contributed to sustainable knowledge transfer, development opportunities and improved skills and job prospects by training 270 employees, of which 200 existing and 70 new employees. Furthermore, the implementation of the new HRM system, talent program and empowering culture change resulted in strongly improved retention rates, 70 new jobs, 12.5 % job growth, increased mobility within the organisation and increased number of promotions.</narrative>
  </description>
